cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Starpi in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Starpi"
abstract: "Knowledge assistant in the browser that shows how far each answer can be trusted: retrieval-augmented generation with verifiable citations, a deterministic source check that compares every statement with the excerpts it cites (facts, reversed negations, and names and values in the wrong place), answer receipts with a Merkle tree and optional signatures that anyone can verify against the original files, and a command that checks documents in CI and writes SARIF. Files are read on the device; answers come from a model chosen for the device (WebGPU or WebAssembly inference in a Web Worker), NVIDIA NIM cloud models through a server-side proxy with a pool of keys, an own server or a cloud model, in a verified source mode or a free chat mode."
authors:
